      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you Francois! We should put this mode use under a build flag which I have added here: https://r.android.com/3341296. The fallback (hybrid mode) should be enabled only when this flag is set to `false`. For that, we need to add a declaration into the Android.bp file to enable a preprocessor define when this flag is `false`:\n\n```\n    cflags: [\n    ...\n    ] + select(release_flag(\"RELEASE_HARDWARE_AUDIO_USE_CAP_AIDL\"), {\n        true: [],\n        default: [\"-DENABLE_CAP_AIDL_HYBRID_MODE\"],\n    }),\n```\n\nI also have a question: can the same XML CAP config files used in both scenarios? If not, then we need to use the flag for picking up appropriate files during build time.",
